[[{"number":4,"state":"open","dependency":{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"manifest_path":"frontend/marketops-console/package-lock.json","scope":"development","relationship":"transitive"},"security_advisory":{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-jqff-g426-hqxp","cve_id":"CVE-2026-76172","summary":"fast-uri vulnerable to host confusion via percent-encoded scheme normalization","description":"### Impact\n\n`fast-uri` decodes percent-encoded characters in the scheme component with the legacy global `unescape()` and serializes the result back as raw characters, without re-escaping it or validating it as a scheme. A scheme that decodes to characters outside the RFC 3986 scheme grammar can therefore introduce structure the original input did not contain.\n\nFor example, `%2f%2fevil.example:/pwn` parses with no authority (`parse().host` is `undefined`), but `resolve()` and `normalize()` return `//evil.example:/pwn`, which reparses with host `evil.example`. The `%uXXXX` form (`%u002f%u002fevil.example:/pwn`) produces the same result, and a scheme containing `%0d%0a` reaches the output as a raw CR LF.\n\nApplications that normalize or resolve untrusted URLs before a redirect check, host allowlist, or outbound request decision, especially ones that treat a missing authority as same-origin, can be steered to an attacker-chosen authority, and a normalized URI placed in a response header can carry an injected CR LF.\n\n### Patches\n\nUpgrade to `fast-uri` >= 4.1.3, or >= 3.1.6 in the v3.x release line, or >= 2.4.5 in the v2.x release line.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nNone. Upgrade to the patched version.","severity":"high","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-jqff-g426-hqxp","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-76172","type":"CVE"}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-jqff-g426-hqxp"},{"url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-76172"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/37f3417c82994279656854f83ce938acd81c3862"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/a941e626411f576f8d90883231e57b6c9d0ff98b"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/c6a74bfd9d8c6b0df5362b3c7ae88d8021cb1e39"},{"url":"https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v2.4.5"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v3.1.6"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v4.1.3"},{"url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jqff-g426-hqxp"}],"published_at":"2026-09-02T15:41:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-02T15:41:56Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 2.3.1, < 2.4.5","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"2.4.5"}},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 3.0.0, < 3.1.6","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"3.1.6"}},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 4.0.0, < 4.1.3","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"4.1.3"}}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","score":7.5},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"epss":{"percentage":0.00232,"percentile":0.13893},"cvss":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","score":7.5},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-177","name":"Improper Handling of URL Encoding (Hex Encoding)"}],"classification":"general"},"security_vulnerability":{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 3.0.0, < 3.1.6","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"3.1.6"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/dependabot/alerts/4","html_url":"https://github.com/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/security/dependabot/4","created_at":"2026-09-03T22:34:00Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T22:34:00Z","dismissal_request":null,"assignees":[],"dismissed_at":null,"dismissed_by":null,"dismissed_reason":null,"dismissed_comment":null,"fixed_at":null,"auto_dismissed_at":null},{"number":3,"state":"open","dependency":{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"manifest_path":"frontend/marketops-console/package-lock.json","scope":"development","relationship":"transitive"},"security_advisory":{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-f65p-4m7j-42xc","cve_id":"CVE-2026-75975","summary":"fast-uri vulnerable to server-side request forgery via malformed IPv6 normalization","description":"### Impact\n\n`fast-uri` does not validate the complete RFC 3986 grammar for bracketed IPv6 literals, so a malformed literal with invalid trailing text is silently truncated to a different valid IPv6 address with no error reported. For example, `normalize('http://[::not-valid]/private')` returns `http://[::]/private`, and `[fc00::not-hex]` and `[fe80::not-hex]` collapse to `[fc00::]` and `[fe80::]`. An application that normalizes an untrusted URL before an outbound request, redirect, or host-policy check can be routed to a local or private address such as loopback (`::1`), unique-local, or link-local. Because `parse().error` is unset for these inputs, checking it does not protect the consumer.\n\n### Patches\n\nUpgrade to `fast-uri` 2.4.5, 3.1.6, or 4.1.3. Malformed IPv6 literals are now rejected with a host error instead of being normalized to a valid address.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nReject untrusted URLs whose host is a bracketed IPv6 literal before passing them to `fast-uri`, or route outbound requests against an explicit allowlist of addresses rather than trusting the normalized host.","severity":"high","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-f65p-4m7j-42xc","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-75975","type":"CVE"}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-f65p-4m7j-42xc"},{"url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-75975"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/3728465caacef4b16bc84b7d14760f1c8fe41595"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/607bfbe953f28a14c2e06ae64aff38c81ca2937f"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/9161eded1ff55fad9d9714c6ad6c0f0283547799"},{"url":"https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v2.4.5"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v3.1.6"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v4.1.3"},{"url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-f65p-4m7j-42xc"}],"published_at":"2026-09-02T15:43:30Z","updated_at":"2026-09-02T15:43:32Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 2.3.1, < 2.4.5","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"2.4.5"}},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 3.0.0, < 3.1.6","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"3.1.6"}},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 4.0.0, < 4.1.3","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"4.1.3"}}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","score":7.5},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"epss":{"percentage":0.0022,"percentile":0.12328},"cvss":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","score":7.5},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-20","name":"Improper Input Validation"},{"cwe_id":"CWE-918","name":"Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)"}],"classification":"general"},"security_vulnerability":{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 3.0.0, < 3.1.6","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"3.1.6"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/dependabot/alerts/3","html_url":"https://github.com/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/security/dependabot/3","created_at":"2026-09-03T21:24:10Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T21:24:10Z","dismissal_request":null,"assignees":[],"dismissed_at":null,"dismissed_by":null,"dismissed_reason":null,"dismissed_comment":null,"fixed_at":null,"auto_dismissed_at":null},{"number":2,"state":"open","dependency":{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"manifest_path":"frontend/marketops-console/package-lock.json","scope":"development","relationship":"transitive"},"security_advisory":{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-fph4-wmhf-6fwf","cve_id":"CVE-2026-75899","summary":"fast-uri vulnerable to server-side request forgery via repeated hostname percent-decoding","description":"### Impact\n\n`fast-uri` decodes a hostname's percent escapes twice in a single `normalize()` or `resolve()` call: once during parsing and again during authority recomposition. A nested percent-encoded host therefore survives the first decode and is turned into a live destination by the second, so `normalize('http://%256c%256f%2563%2561%256c%2568%256f%2573%2574/')` returns `http://localhost/`. Applications that normalize or resolve an untrusted URI before an SSRF check, redirect validation, or host allowlist can be steered to a different destination, including internal addresses such as loopback or a cloud metadata endpoint, than the encoded input appeared to contain. This is an incomplete-fix variant of CVE-2026-6322, whose encoded-authority-delimiter fix introduced the second decode.\n\n### Patches\n\nFixed in `fast-uri` 2.4.5, 3.1.6, and 4.1.3.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nReject untrusted URIs whose host component contains an encoded percent sign (`%25`) before passing them to `normalize()` or `resolve()`.","severity":"high","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-fph4-wmhf-6fwf","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-75899","type":"CVE"}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-fph4-wmhf-6fwf"},{"url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-75899"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/2642290672e7211c990aaed3749c2ce667d0af4f"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/8c15dbe94ec50bb8e595791ebb42c35cef0fd304"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/ae92a4c5d8c4b6c9e447f048d5fcbde7eebd5514"},{"url":"https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v2.4.5"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v3.1.6"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v4.1.3"},{"url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-fph4-wmhf-6fwf"}],"published_at":"2026-09-02T15:42:39Z","updated_at":"2026-09-02T15:42:41Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 2.4.1, < 2.4.5","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"2.4.5"}},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 3.1.2, < 3.1.6","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"3.1.6"}},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 4.0.0, < 4.1.3","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"4.1.3"}}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","score":7.5},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"epss":{"percentage":0.0022,"percentile":0.12328},"cvss":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","score":7.5},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-174","name":"Double Decoding of the Same Data"},{"cwe_id":"CWE-918","name":"Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)"}],"classification":"general"},"security_vulnerability":{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 3.1.2, < 3.1.6","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"3.1.6"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/dependabot/alerts/2","html_url":"https://github.com/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/security/dependabot/2","created_at":"2026-09-03T07:45:11Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T07:45:11Z","dismissal_request":null,"assignees":[],"dismissed_at":null,"dismissed_by":null,"dismissed_reason":null,"dismissed_comment":null,"fixed_at":null,"auto_dismissed_at":null},{"number":1,"state":"open","dependency":{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"manifest_path":"frontend/marketops-console/package-lock.json","scope":"development","relationship":"transitive"},"security_advisory":{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-5jgf-p345-68v8","cve_id":"CVE-2026-75931","summary":"fast-uri vulnerable to host confusion via skipped IDN canonicalization on scheme-relative references","description":"### Impact\n\n`fast-uri` canonicalizes a host to its ASCII form only when the input carries an explicit scheme. When `resolve()` resolves a scheme-relative reference (`//host/`) against a scheme-bearing base, it still emits the host verbatim even though the effective scheme is known, so re-parsing the resolved URI yields a different host than the one `resolve()` returned. An application that resolves an untrusted reference with `fast-uri` and then checks or routes on the resulting host can make a policy decision on one host and reach another. This is an incomplete-fix variant of CVE-2026-13676, whose IDN canonicalization was applied only to the scheme-bearing form.\n\n### Patches\n\nUpgrade to `fast-uri` 2.4.5, 3.1.6, or 4.1.3. `resolve()` now canonicalizes the host once the effective scheme is known, and fails closed if a raw non-ASCII host cannot be converted.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nResolve scheme-relative references against a base that carries a scheme before performing any host-policy or origin check.","severity":"high","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-5jgf-p345-68v8","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-75931","type":"CVE"}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-5jgf-p345-68v8"},{"url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-75931"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/0256bc8d1f28b5d0ac657faf67e2411a189dfcb5"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/444ecdad447db2cc23c4d422acc6f0daa6fa8eef"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/4e4ebd8b245f6ca16e448203559eea3e545453a3"},{"url":"https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v2.4.5"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v3.1.6"},{"url":"https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v4.1.3"},{"url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5jgf-p345-68v8"}],"published_at":"2026-09-02T15:44:30Z","updated_at":"2026-09-02T15:44:32Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 2.4.2, < 2.4.5","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"2.4.5"}},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 3.1.3, < 3.1.6","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"3.1.6"}},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 4.0.1, < 4.1.3","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"4.1.3"}}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","score":7.5},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"epss":{"percentage":0.00232,"percentile":0.13894},"cvss":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","score":7.5},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-436","name":"Interpretation Conflict"}],"classification":"general"},"security_vulnerability":{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"fast-uri"},"severity":"high","vulnerable_version_range":">= 3.1.3, < 3.1.6","first_patched_version":{"identifier":"3.1.6"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/dependabot/alerts/1","html_url":"https://github.com/Corwin-Code/marketops-platform/security/dependabot/1","created_at":"2026-09-03T04:29:06Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T04:29:06Z","dismissal_request":null,"assignees":[],"dismissed_at":null,"dismissed_by":null,"dismissed_reason":null,"dismissed_comment":null,"fixed_at":null,"auto_dismissed_at":null}]]